# Review transcripts are evidence for us and noise for everyone else: they carry
# absolute local paths, prior prompts and tool output. They stay in the repo
# because PROGRESS.md and the numbered plans cite them, but no archive of this
# tree — however it is produced — should ever ship them.
*-codex-*.log export-ignore
*-review.log export-ignore

# The numbered documents are the working history of this project: plans,
# pricing, business model, network topology, and the names of the instances it
# runs on. They cite each other and the transcripts above, so they stay in the
# private repository — but 83 lines across 20 of them name clients, the
# production hostname and the VPS address, and `git archive HEAD` is how this
# tree becomes the public release. Measured, not assumed: extract the archive
# and grep before changing this list.
[0-9][0-9]-*.md export-ignore
PROGRESS.md export-ignore
CLAUDE.md export-ignore
AGENTS.md export-ignore
CODEX-TASK-2-parsers.md export-ignore
